 "calibration": "PROVISIONAL: the iPhone clips decide the final values. Thresholds: the public-clip Gate 2 candidate (docs/experiments/asl-model-probe.md Run 5, 28 Oct 2026), global p 0.65 plus per-word cut-offs, fitted and scored on the same public clips. Vocabulary: only the rehearsed words, minus morning (the model learned a one-handed MORNING; it stays out until the iPhone test), because every confident wrong chip on the public clips was an unrehearsed vocabulary gloss (can, hungry, time). Rule: full 250-way softmax, never restricted to the vocabulary first; chip when top-1 is in the vocabulary, p >= thresholds.p (or per_word[gloss]) and margin >= thresholds.margin; pick-one when top-1 is in the vocabulary and pick_one_p <= p < the chip cut-off; otherwise unsure."
